// Surface code - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

// The surface code is not a program: it is a description of a
// quantum error-correcting layout -- a grid of data qubits and
// syndrome qubits whose stabilizers are measured over and over.
// Nothing executes and nothing prints, so the greeting is here.
// Hello World!
// distance d, repeated round: measure stabilizers, correct, repeat.
